/// The wire error code this service answers an authorization refusal with.
///
/// NOT a shape in this service's model (`smithy_query(query="operation",
/// operation="AssociateUser")` lists only AccessDeniedException / ConflictException /
/// InternalServerException / ResourceNotFoundException / ServiceQuotaExceededException /
/// ThrottlingException / ValidationException), so it cannot be a variant of any
/// generated error enum — hence [`ServiceRefusal`] below. It is the code the recorded
/// wire carries for a request this service will not confirm the caller's ownership of.
pub const UNAUTHORIZED_EXCEPTION_CODE: &str = "UnauthorizedException";

/// The FIXED sentence that travels with [`UNAUTHORIZED_EXCEPTION_CODE`].
///
/// One sentence for every such refusal, carrying nothing from the request: a fail-closed
/// refusal must not disclose whether the identifier it was asked about names anything.
pub const UNAUTHORIZED_EXCEPTION_MESSAGE: &str =
    "Unauthorized. Please check the request and access policy and try again.";

/// The HTTP status [`UNAUTHORIZED_EXCEPTION_CODE`] is reported with.
///
/// 401, the status the recorded wire carries for it. This code is in NO model, so it
/// inherits nothing from the 400 the service's modelled client errors default to: the
/// refusal states that the caller may not act on the resource it named, which is the
/// outcome a client branches on — an authorization branch (refresh credentials, re-authorize,
/// pick another resource), not the malformed-request branch a 400 selects. It is still a
/// client-fault status rather than a 5xx an SDK retry classifier would retry: the refusal is
/// terminal until the caller changes the request or its access.
pub const UNAUTHORIZED_EXCEPTION_STATUS: u16 = 401;

/// The wire error code an authorization refusal — the decision of the IAM layer in FRONT
/// of this service — travels under.
///
/// `AccessDeniedException` is a shape of this service's model ("You don't have sufficient
/// access to perform this action.") and all but its three tagging operations declare it,
/// but the decision is taken before a request is routed to one operation
/// ([`crate::service`]'s authorization gate), so it is answered through [`ServiceRefusal`]
/// — the one channel that carries a code and a status without belonging to one operation's
/// generated enum. The code and the body a caller sees are the modelled ones either way.
pub const ACCESS_DENIED_EXCEPTION_CODE: &str = "AccessDeniedException";

/// The HTTP status [`ACCESS_DENIED_EXCEPTION_CODE`] is reported with: 400, the status the
/// model gives that error (`smithy_query(query="shape",shape="AccessDeniedException")` —
/// `errorKind` client with no `@httpError`, which defaults to 400), so a refusal answered
/// ahead of the operation carries exactly the status the operation's own modelled variant
/// would.
pub const ACCESS_DENIED_EXCEPTION_STATUS: u16 = 400;

/// The wire error code this service's TAGGING surface answers an unresolvable
/// `ResourceArn` with — also not a shape in this service's model (`UntagResource` models
/// only InternalServerException and ResourceNotFoundException).
pub const BAD_REQUEST_EXCEPTION_CODE: &str = "BadRequestException";

/// The FIXED sentence that travels with [`BAD_REQUEST_EXCEPTION_CODE`] for a
/// `ResourceArn` naming no resource this service holds.
pub const INVALID_INPUT_RESOURCE_ARN_MESSAGE: &str = "Invalid input resource arn";

/// The FIXED sentence that travels with [`BAD_REQUEST_EXCEPTION_CODE`] for a
